    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear strategy: exploit the favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt and Bubba Chandler to bolster our offensive ceiling. **Kyle Tucker** (75.29) and **Andy Pages** (70.97) anchor our lineup, benefiting immensely from Pfaadt\u2019s 4.54 xERA and their high-probability stolen base environments\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on speed. **Jacob Wilson** (69.79) also presents an elite start, taking advantage of a positive park factor and a favorable platoon look against a lefty starter. These players represent our core efficiency drivers, as their combination of order position and matchup softness provides the high floor we require for 5x5 accumulation.\n\nWhile the primary lineup is optimized for production, the decision to bench **Sam Antonacci** (46.73) remains the most difficult exclusion of the day. Despite his encouraging base projection, the matchup against a high-tier arm like Gavin Williams\u2014coupled with a significant SP skill handicap\u2014pushed his score just below our threshold for starting consideration. Furthermore, we must monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson** (60.75) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (63.18) closely. Both are facing elite arms in Jacob deGrom and Bubba Chandler, respectively; while **Gunnar Henderson** fights through a massive 19% SP skill penalty, his dynamic platoon advantage helps maintain his score. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** carries risk due to the platoon adjustment, but we are banking on his ability to capitalize on Chandler\u2019s slow delivery to pad our stolen base category. Be advised that several slots\u2014including **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**\u2014are contingent on \"Lineup Pending\" status; we must be prepared to adjust if their official batting order shifts significantly from our current projections.",
